# JavaScript Async Interview — Today's Questions & Answers

## 1. Event Loop: Callback + Promise + Async/Await

### Question

```js
console.log("A");

setTimeout(() => {
    console.log("B");
}, 0);

Promise.resolve().then(() => {
    console.log("C");

    setTimeout(() => {
        console.log("D");
    }, 0);
});

async function test() {
    console.log("E");

    await Promise.resolve();

    console.log("F");
}

test();

console.log("G");
```

### Correct answer

```text
A
E
G
C
F
B
D
```

### Why?

Synchronous code executes first:

```text
A
E
G
```

Then microtasks:

```text
C
F
```

Then timers:

```text
B
D
```

### Key rule

```text
Synchronous code
       ↓
Microtasks (.then, await continuation)
       ↓
Macrotasks (setTimeout)
```

