# 5. Promise.allSettled()

### Question

```js
const requests = [
    Promise.resolve("User"),
    Promise.reject("Orders failed"),
    Promise.resolve("Products"),
    Promise.reject("Payments failed")
];

Promise.allSettled(requests).then(result => {
    console.log(result);
});
```

### Correct output structure

```js
[
    {
        status: "fulfilled",
        value: "User"
    },
    {
        status: "rejected",
        reason: "Orders failed"
    },
    {
        status: "fulfilled",
        value: "Products"
    },
    {
        status: "rejected",
        reason: "Payments failed"
    }
]
```

### Why use `allSettled()`?

Suppose a dashboard has:

```text
User       ✅
Orders     ❌
Products   ✅
Payments   ❌
```

You still want the successful data.

`Promise.all()` would reject the whole operation.

`Promise.allSettled()` tells you the result of **every Promise**.

