# 6. Promise.race()

### Question 1

```js
const fastSuccess = new Promise(resolve => {
    setTimeout(() => resolve("SUCCESS"), 1000);
});

const slowFailure = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    setTimeout(() => reject("FAILED"), 3000);
});

Promise.race([fastSuccess, slowFailure])
    .then(result => console.log("THEN:", result))
    .catch(error => console.log("CATCH:", error));
```

### Answer

After 1 second:

```text
THEN: SUCCESS
```

---

### Question 2

```js
const fastFailure = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    setTimeout(() => reject("FAILED"), 1000);
});

const slowSuccess = new Promise(resolve => {
    setTimeout(() => resolve("SUCCESS"), 3000);
});

Promise.race([fastFailure, slowSuccess])
    .then(result => console.log("THEN:", result))
    .catch(error => console.log("CATCH:", error));
```

### Answer

After 1 second:

```text
CATCH: FAILED
```

### Critical interview concept

`Promise.race()` does **NOT** mean:

> First successful Promise wins.

It means:

> **First settled Promise wins.**

Settled means:

```text
fulfilled OR rejected
```

