# 10. Promise.all vs allSettled vs race vs any

This is one of the most important interview tables.

| Method         | Waits for       | Rejects?                           | Returns              |
| -------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------- |
| `all()`        | All             | If any rejects                     | Array                |
| `allSettled()` | All             | ❌ Never because of input rejection | Array                |
| `race()`       | First settled   | If first settled rejects           | Single result/reason |
| `any()`        | First fulfilled | Only if **all** reject             | Single value         |

### Example

```text
Promise.all()
A ✅ B ✅ C ✅
→ [A, B, C]

Promise.allSettled()
A ✅ B ❌ C ✅
→ [{...}, {...}, {...}]

Promise.race()
A finishes first
→ A

Promise.any()
A ❌ B ❌ C ✅
→ C
```

